	(text "Yaesu AC (G-450 class): land motor CW (Yaesu 5) on J1-5, motor CCW (Yaesu 4) on J1-6,\nmotor common (Yaesu 6) and pot ground (Yaesu 3) on J1-1, pot REF (Yaesu 1) on J1-3,\npot wiper (Yaesu 2) on J1-7. Open SJ1/SJ2, close SJ3/SJ4 so the cap sits across the drive ends.\nG-5500 and HDR-300 keep the cap in the rotor: leave SJ1-SJ4 open and do not fit C1/C2.\nHDR-300's pinout is not this 1:1 map. It needs a cable adapter. Cap omitted either way.\nBrake enable AZ_BRAKE_EN high RELEASES the brake. Any fault or ARM drop engages it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 229.87 50.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4 1.4)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "34bd69bb-45ff-4318-9599-add6f096fb79")
	)
	(text "26 VAC inlet, fuse, MOV, half-wave tap, current transformer, ARM relay. Logic stays up when ARM opens."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 270.256 89.408 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "3d01385d-11fe-4ac6-94dc-7a95f2f5e1e6")
	)
	(text "Each channel, left to right: 180 ohm from +5V, red LED (anode toward the resistor), MOC3023SM,\n2N7002 to ROTOR_RETURN. Below: 100 ohm gate, 1k gate-to-MT1, BTA16-600SW, 68 ohm + 0.1 uF X2,\nLTV-814 stuck-on sense. Triacs stand vertical on the bar, 12.7 mm pitch, lead row near board x 34.4."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 655.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4 1.4)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "4d1ef98b-5179-433d-8bac-2e9abf0cfc27")
	)
	(text "Interlock, 3.3 V. CW_GATE = CW_EN AND NOT CCW_EN AND ARM_OK AND NOT HOLD_CCW.\nARM_OK = ARM_EN AND nRESET. BRK_GATE = AZ_BRAKE_EN AND ARM_OK.\nHOLD is about 70-110 ms (1 uF, 100k, 74LVC14). See DESIGN-NOTES.md."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 420.37 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4 1.4)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "510b4706-c3e3-46f4-b426-e93f70298259")
	)
	(text "CDE terminal block J1, 1:1 with the rotor strip (catalog hygain-ham-iv, V4 sheet note).\n1 ROTOR_RETURN  common: motor, brake, pot wiper\n2 BRAKE         solenoid. Energized = released. Off = wedge engaged\n3 AZ_POT_3      pot end +\n4 CAP / winding end. Run cap across 4 and 8 for CDE (SJ1, SJ2 bridged)\n5 CW            via the right limit switch to terminal 8\n6 CCW           via the left limit switch to terminal 4\n7 AZ_POT_7      pot end -\n8 CAP / winding end\nV4's J3 is a 10-pin Mate-N-Lok. Its pin numbers are not these terminal numbers.\nThe V4 text note (1 Return, 2 Brake, 4 Cap Left, 5 Motor Right, 6 Motor Left, 8 Cap Right)\nmatches this map. Right = CW, Left = CCW."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 50.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4 1.4)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "9fcc164c-5e9a-4229-83f1-f02c5e68c5b4")
	)
	(text "ROTOR INTERFACE AND AC MOTOR DRIVE  (azimuth, AC version)\nF407 controller, first sheet. MCU pin assignment is deferred.\nLogic ground is ROTOR_RETURN (CDE terminal 1). See DESIGN-NOTES.md and ADR 0018.\nHierarchical labels leave this sheet for the processor sheet and the power sheet."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "ec687124-ab51-40d9-b428-51bb26b3a492")
	)
